"id": "e6714c6b-2159-482b-8ab7-5809476684cb",
"title": "Costs of treatment",
"slug": "costs-of-treatment",
"lang": "en",


{
"id": "e6714c6b-2159-482b-8ab7-5809476684cb",
"title": "Costs of treatment",
"slug": "costs-of-treatment",
"lang": "en",
"content": {
"blocks": [
{
"type": "divider"
},
{
"text": "How much the treatment costs",
"type": "heading",
"level": 2
},
{
"text": "Brain tumor treatment costs worldwide range widely from $5,000 to over $150,000, heavily depending on the country, hospital type, tumor complexity, and whether it requires surgery, radiation, or chemotherapy. Western nations like the United States are the most expensive, while countries like India, Egypt, and Turkey offer more affordable medical travel options.",
"type": "paragraph"
},
{
"alt": " BLK-Max Super Speciality Hospital | Delhi, India",
"src": "https://static.medigence.com/uploads/hospital/images/1743434712_9a1dbd46f3aeafcb9de7.jpg",
"type": "image"
},
{
"text": "Estimated Cost by Country",
"type": "heading",
"level": 2
},
{
"type": "list",
"items": [
"United States: $80,000 – $150,000+ (total care including follow-ups and complications can exceed $500,000)",
"Germany: $25,000 – $55,000",
"Thailand: $18,000 – $32,000",
"United Arab Emirates: $15,000 – $50,000",
"Turkey: $10,000 – $22,000",
"India: $5,000 – $15,000 (approx. ₹2,50,000 – ₹7,50,000)",
"Egypt: $5,000 – $12,000"
],
"ordered": false
},
{
"type": "divider"
},
{
"text": "Key Cost Factors",
"type": "heading",
"level": 2
},
{
"type": "list",
"items": [
"Type of Procedure: A standard craniotomy for surgical removal is different from non-invasive options like CyberKnife or Gamma Knife radiosurgery.",
"Additional Therapies: Post-operative radiation therapy, chemotherapy, or targeted therapy add separate costs.",
"Hospital Stay & ICU: Extended intensive care unit (ICU) days and specialized implants increase the final bill.",
"Diagnostics: Pre-surgery and post-surgery MRI scans, CT scans, and biopsies contribute to the overall expenditure."
],
"ordered": false
},
{
"type": "divider"
},
{
"text": "Are you looking for treatment costs in a specific city or country, or do you need details about a particular type of brain tumor or procedure?",
"type": "quote"
},
{
"type": "divider"
},
{
"text": "Are you looking for treatment costs in a specific city or country, or do you need details about a particular type of brain tumor or procedure?",
"type": "callout",
"variant": "bad",
"textColor": "#c061cb",
"borderColor": "#62a0ea",
"backgroundColor": "#f5c211"
},
{
"src": "/uploads/3b925bd7575b4d9c94c6553c8b294340.mp4",
"type": "video",
"controls": true
}
],
"format": "blocks-v1"
},
"content_text": "How much the treatment costs Brain tumor treatment costs worldwide range widely from $5,000 to over $150,000, heavily depending on the country, hospital type, tumor complexity, and whether it requires surgery, radiation, or chemotherapy. Western nations like the United States are the most expensive, while countries like India, Egypt, and Turkey offer more affordable medical travel options. BLK-Max Super Speciality Hospital | Delhi, India Estimated Cost by Country United States: $80,000 – $150,000+ (total care including follow-ups and complications can exceed $500,000) Germany: $25,000 – $55,000 Thailand: $18,000 – $32,000 United Arab Emirates: $15,000 – $50,000 Turkey: $10,000 – $22,000 India: $5,000 – $15,000 (approx. ₹2,50,000 – ₹7,50,000) Egypt: $5,000 – $12,000 Key Cost Factors Type of Procedure: A standard craniotomy for surgical removal is different from non-invasive options like CyberKnife or Gamma Knife radiosurgery. Additional Therapies: Post-operative radiation therapy, chemotherapy, or targeted therapy add separate costs. Hospital Stay & ICU: Extended intensive care unit (ICU) days and specialized implants increase the final bill. Diagnostics: Pre-surgery and post-surgery MRI scans, CT scans, and biopsies contribute to the overall expenditure. Are you looking for treatment costs in a specific city or country, or do you need details about a particular type of brain tumor or procedure? Are you looking for treatment costs in a specific city or country, or do you need details about a particular type of brain tumor or procedure?",
